# =============================================================================
# CommitAI web app — PRODUCTION environment template
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Copy the values into your host's env / secret manager (Vercel, Fly, Railway,
# Docker secrets, etc.). Do NOT commit a filled-in copy — real secrets live only
# in the host. The four keys marked "SECRET" must come from a secret store, never
# from the repo. See `.env.example` for the full field-by-field documentation;
# this file is the production checklist + production-appropriate defaults.
#
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PRE-DEPLOY CHECKLIST (do these in order — see README / LIMITATIONS.md)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  [ ] 1. ROTATE the leaked GitHub PAT (revoke ghp_… at
#         https://github.com/settings/tokens) and any other exposed credential
#         BEFORE deploying. Never reuse a token that has appeared in plaintext.
#  [ ] 2. Provision a reachable Postgres and set DATABASE_URL (below), then apply
#         migrations:  pnpm --filter web exec prisma migrate deploy
#  [ ] 3. Set the four remaining SECRETS: GEMINI_API_KEY, SESSION_PASSWORD,
#         ATTESTOR_PRIVATE_KEY, AI_VERIFIER_PRIVATE_KEY (see notes on each).
#  [ ] 4. Confirm the deployed CommitmentVault matches the current contract
#         source (the escrow fix in commit cc3fc3a, and the item-11 signed-receipt
#         approveCompletion). If the live bytecode predates either, redeploy the
#         vault (contracts/DEPLOY.md) and update COMMITMENT_VAULT_ADDRESS below.
#         The redeploy also sets INITIAL_AI_VERIFIER — it must match the address of
#         AI_VERIFIER_PRIVATE_KEY, or every approval reverts (fail-closed).
#  [ ] 5. Point APP_ORIGIN / NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL at the real https origin.
#  [ ] 6. Re-run the suite against the prod DB + real GEMINI_API_KEY so the
#         DB-gated + Gemini + cross-wallet tests actually execute (they SKIP when
#         those deps are absent):  pnpm --filter web test
#  [ ] 7. Build:  pnpm --filter web build   (must exit 0)
# =============================================================================

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SECRET — PostgreSQL (Prisma). Must be reachable; migrations must be applied.
# Use a pooled connection string in serverless environments.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@DB_HOST:5432/commitai?schema=public&sslmode=require"
# Optional: a direct (non-pooled) URL for `prisma migrate` if your pooler needs it.
# DIRECT_URL="postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@DB_HOST:5432/commitai?schema=public&sslmode=require"

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SECRET — Gemini (AI verification). REQUIRED in prod; without it verification is
# disabled and its tests skip. This is the MODEL key only, never a wallet/deployer
# key (CLAUDE.md §3).
#
# TIER: the FREE tier is a deliberate, documented choice (LIMITATIONS.md §10.1,
# item 13), not an oversight. On it Google may use prompts/responses to improve
# their products — which is acceptable here ONLY because no raw evidence is ever
# sent to the model: uploaded bytes, Evidence.contentText and blob storage keys are
# unreachable from lib/ai/, enforced by 11 always-on tests in
# lib/ai/privacyBoundary.test.ts. The model sees goal/verification metadata, hashes,
# and the user's own chat text.
#
# A paid tier (data excluded from training) or self-hosted inference behind the same
# AIProvider interface is still the recommended production upgrade — it removes the
# training caveat on the user's own chat text. It changes no code above gemini.ts,
# and it is NOT required for the evidence-privacy guarantee, which holds as-is.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
GEMINI_API_KEY=""
GEMINI_MODEL="gemini-3.7-flash"

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SECRET — iron-session cookie encryption key, min 32 chars. The server refuses
# to open a session without it (no weak fallback). Generate:  openssl rand -base64 32
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
SESSION_PASSWORD=""

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SECRET — backend attestor key. Server-only. MONEY-SAFETY (CLAUDE.md §2–3):
# this key can ONLY attest (registerMilestone / requestCompletion /
# approveCompletion / setAttestor) — no code path moves depositor funds; every
# transfer is depositor-signed and pull-based. NEVER a deployer/wallet key.
# It cannot approve a completion alone — see AI_VERIFIER_PRIVATE_KEY below.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
ATTESTOR_PRIVATE_KEY=""

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SECRET — AI verifier key. Server-only, SIGNING ONLY (LIMITATIONS.md item 11).
# Approval is two-of-two: the attestor SENDS approveCompletion, this key SIGNS the
# EIP-712 VerificationReceipt over {commitmentId, goalId, milestoneRef, confidence,
# evidenceHash, verificationHash, modelVersionHash, deadline}, and the contract
# reverts unless the recovered signer is exactly the on-chain aiVerifier.
# MONEY-SAFETY: getReceiptSigner() is a frozen { address, signReceipt } — no wallet
# client, no transport, no writeContract/sendTransaction (receipt.safety.test.ts) —
# so it cannot send a transaction at all. Its address MUST equal the vault's
# aiVerifier() and MUST differ from the attestor's. NEVER a deployer/wallet key.
# Rotate via setAiVerifier() from the owner Safe; rotation retires old receipts.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
AI_VERIFIER_PRIVATE_KEY=""

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# On-chain: BOT Chain testnet + CommitmentVault. These are PUBLIC (not secrets).
# Verify COMMITMENT_VAULT_ADDRESS matches the fixed source before going live
# (checklist item 4); a set-but-malformed address fails loudly rather than
# degrading to a default.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
BOTCHAIN_TESTNET_RPC_URL="https://rpc.bohr.life"
BOTCHAIN_TESTNET_CHAIN_ID="968"
BOTCHAIN_TESTNET_EXPLORER_URL="https://scan.bohr.life"
COMMITMENT_VAULT_ADDRESS="0x0076c4269be298429af7827a2a5cc40a65f8f8a8"

# Block the vault was deployed in. Sets where a historical event replay starts
# (POST /api/chain/reconcile, LIMITATIONS.md item 12) so the reconciler need not
# scan from genesis. Optional, not a secret; unset = start at block 0. Set it to the
# block of the deploy tx you record in README.md, and re-set it after any redeploy —
# a stale value pointing BEFORE the current vault is merely slow, never wrong.
# Set-but-malformed fails loudly.
COMMITMENT_VAULT_DEPLOYMENT_BLOCK=""

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Evidence storage. Raw evidence stays OFF-chain (only its sha256 is eligible for
# anchoring). "local" writes to disk — for a multi-instance / serverless deploy,
# either point EVIDENCE_STORAGE_DIR at a persistent, writable volume (ephemeral FS
# loses blobs) or use the "s3" driver against an S3-compatible bucket (AWS S3,
# Supabase Storage, R2, MinIO). Both are the same content-addressed interface (§13).
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
EVIDENCE_STORAGE_DRIVER="local"
EVIDENCE_STORAGE_DIR="/var/lib/commitai/evidence-store"

# For EVIDENCE_STORAGE_DRIVER="s3": bucket + region required; endpoint optional for
# AWS, required for Supabase/R2/MinIO. Credentials move blobs only, never funds.
# EVIDENCE_S3_BUCKET="commitai-evidence"
# EVIDENCE_S3_REGION="us-east-1"
# EVIDENCE_S3_ENDPOINT="https://<project>.supabase.co/storage/v1/s3"
# EVIDENCE_S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID=""
# EVIDENCE_S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=""

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Evidence content hardening (§13, item 10). Sniffing + EXIF/metadata scrubbing are
# always on. Malware scanning is opt-in: leave "off" and uploads are stored
# unscanned (honestly reported as such), or point it at a real ClamAV daemon — after
# which it is FAIL-CLOSED, so a scanner outage refuses uploads (503) rather than
# storing them unscanned. Recommended for a public deployment.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
EVIDENCE_MALWARE_SCAN="off"
# EVIDENCE_MALWARE_SCAN="clamd"
# EVIDENCE_CLAMD_HOST="clamav"
# EVIDENCE_CLAMD_PORT="3310"
# EVIDENCE_CLAMD_TIMEOUT_MS="10000"

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# App origin + SIWE session domain. Set to the REAL https origin: used for the
# same-origin/CSRF check and the expected SIWE domain (anti-phishing).
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
APP_ORIGIN="https://your-domain.example"
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL="https://your-domain.example"

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WalletConnect project id (public, client-exposed — NEXT_PUBLIC_*). Create one
# at https://cloud.reown.com (formerly WalletConnect Cloud). Required for wallet
# connection in the browser.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
NEXT_PUBLIC_WALLETCONNECT_PROJECT_ID=""
